# Every variable the repo reads (codebase-conventions §5). Copy this file to
# apps/web/.env.local and fill the values; turbo.json lists the same names.
# Each comment says what breaks without the variable. Every value below is
# synthetic.
#
# Suffix grammar: a tiered variable ends in _LOCAL or _STAGING; the unsuffixed
# name is production's, and the fallback when a tier's own value is unset.

# Set by Next and Node (development, production, test); never set it. Listed
# because turbo.json keys its cache on it.
# NODE_ENV=

# The tier switch: local | staging | production. Unset means local; production
# is never a default. Without it nothing breaks: the app talks to local services.
DATABASE_ENVIRONMENT=local

# Set by the platform, never by you: production or preview inside a Vercel
# deployment. Unset or development means the code runs locally, so the site URL
# is http://localhost:3000.
# VERCEL_ENV=

# The site's public origin per tier. Without it a deployment has no site URL and
# the build fails validation; locally it is ignored (always localhost).
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://www.example.test
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL_STAGING=https://staging.example.test
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL_LOCAL=http://localhost:3000

# A synthetic server-only secret that proves the picker and the client-bundle
# check (yarn check-client-bundle). Nothing calls it; without it nothing breaks.
# The first vendor ticket replaces it with a real key.
EXAMPLE_API_KEY=example-production-key
EXAMPLE_API_KEY_STAGING=example-staging-key
EXAMPLE_API_KEY_LOCAL=example-local-key

# --- Database (@pem/db, STK-9) ---------------------------------------------
# Runtime URL: the Supabase transaction pooler (port 6543) on a hosted tier.
# Without it, staging and production cannot query the database; on the local
# tier an unset value means the image `yarn db:local` starts.
DATABASE_URL=
DATABASE_URL_LOCAL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:54322/postgres
DATABASE_URL_STAGING=
# Migration URL: the Supabase session pooler (port 5432). Without it,
# `yarn db:migrate` and `yarn db:setup` cannot reach staging or production;
# on the local tier an unset value means the local image.
DATABASE_MIGRATION_URL=
DATABASE_MIGRATION_URL_LOCAL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:54322/postgres
DATABASE_MIGRATION_URL_STAGING=

# Supabase Auth (@pem/auth, STK-12; the local modes are D-STK-6). Read by apps/web/env.ts
# and by yarn db:seed-users. The _LOCAL values select the local mode; there is no mode variable.
#   Mode A, the default (yarn db:local): copy the _STAGING values. Sign-in runs on hosted
#   staging and the local auth mirror copies each signed-in user into the local database.
#   Add http://localhost:3000/auth/callback to the staging project's redirect URLs.
#   Keep each project's email rate limit (Authentication, Rate Limits) set: the sign-in form
#   sends a link to any address it is given, and custom SMTP raises the default.
#   Mode B (yarn db:local:full): the API URL (http://127.0.0.1:54321) and the keys that
#   `yarn workspace @pem/db supabase status` prints.
# Without the URL and the publishable key, the app serves every request signed out and the
# sign-in page says sign-in is not set up. The publishable key (sb_publishable_..., or the
# legacy anon key) is public by design; row-level security guards the data.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL_LOCAL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL_STAGING=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY_LOCAL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY_STAGING=
# The service-role key bypasses row-level security: server-only, never in a NEXT_PUBLIC_
# variable. Without it, @pem/auth's admin client throws and db:seed-users cannot create the
# synthetic local users.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY_LOCAL=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY_STAGING=
# OAuth providers are configured in the Supabase dashboard, not here; the app reads no
# provider variable.

# --- Email (@pem/email, STK-15) --------------------------------------------
# Resend's API key. The local tier never sends (it logs the message), so _LOCAL
# stays empty. Without it a staging or production send throws, naming the variable.
RESEND_API_KEY=
RESEND_API_KEY_STAGING=
# RESEND_API_KEY_LOCAL=
# The sending address, on a domain verified in Resend. Without it the sender is
# @pem/brand's contact address, which Resend refuses unless that domain is verified.
EMAIL_FROM=
EMAIL_FROM_STAGING=
# EMAIL_FROM_LOCAL=

# --- Error monitoring (Sentry, apps/web only; STK-18) ----------------------
# Each tier reports only to its own project and never falls back to
# production's: staging without _STAGING reports nothing. The local tier sends
# nothing unless _LOCAL is set on purpose. The DSN is public by design (it only
# lets a client send events). Without it, errors are logged and not reported.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN_STAGING=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN_LOCAL=
# Derived by env.ts from DATABASE_ENVIRONMENT for the browser; never set it.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_ENVIRONMENT=
# Source-map upload, at build on a deployment only. Without the token, the org
# or the tier's project, the build skips the upload and succeeds; stack traces
# in Sentry then point at minified code. The token is an organization token
# with the project:releases scope; it is secret.
SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN=
SENTRY_ORG=
SENTRY_PROJECT=
SENTRY_PROJECT_STAGING=
# Set by the platform, never by you: the commit Vercel builds, used as the
# Sentry release. Unset, events carry no release.
# VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA=
# Set by Next for each server bundle (nodejs or edge); never set it.
# NEXT_RUNTIME=
